[00:29.71]From northern skerries down the long grey coast
[00:34.19]From every pier and every jut of stone
[00:38.77]A hundred hands do strike a hundred flames
[00:43.29]And the dark doth learneth it shall not reign alone

[00:47.84]The boats go out with lanterns at their prows
[00:52.22]The children run with sparklers on the sand
[00:56.84]And bonfire after bonfire crowns the shore
[01:01.20]Till the whole of the northland burning stand

[01:06.06]Bálit brenna! — the bonfires burneth high!
[01:10.65]Eldr á vatni! — fire upon the sea!

[01:18.57]Light them! Light them! Every fire on the shore!
[01:23.00]Light them till the night doth turneth day!
[01:27.60]Kveikið! Kveikið! Bál við bál!
[01:31.74]Let the whole coast catch and blaze away!
[01:36.55]Eldr! Eldr! Ljós á vatni!
[01:38.95]Strike the spark and let it climb!
[01:41.11]For the summer's end deserveth fire
[01:44.47]And we light it one last time!

[02:03.68]The horn goes round from hand to weathered hand
[02:08.25]The first sparks climb and scatter on the wind
[02:12.80]The elders nod, the young ones cannot wait
[02:17.89]And every heart along the coast doth grin

[02:21.86]Bálit brenna! — the bonfires burneth high!
[02:26.32]Eldr á vatni! — fire upon the sea!

[02:34.40]Light them! Light them! Every fire on the shore!
[02:38.86]Light them till the night doth turneth day!
[02:43.36]Kveikið! Kveikið! Bál við bál!
[02:47.65]Let the whole coast catch and blaze away!
[02:52.45]Eldr! Eldr! Ljós á vatni!
[02:54.76]Strike the spark and let it climb!
[02:56.77]For the summer's end deserveth fire
[03:00.04]And we light it one last time!

[03:10.62]Now the sea is ringed in fire!
[03:15.01]Now the night begins!
[03:17.55]Eldr á vatni! Eldr á vatni!
